---
title: Mitsurugi Cards
nav: mitsurugi-cards
bg: cards
description: Every Mitsurugi card grouped by where it activates in hand, graveyard, or field, plus the archetype's on-tribute triggers, with tips for real games.
---
{% from "components.njk" import synergyCard, cardGroup, zoneFilter, sectionTabs, filterEmpty, cardSearch %}

<section class="container-narrow comp-head">
  <div class="kicker">// CARD COMPENDIUM</div>
  <h1>Every card, by where it activates</h1>
  <p class="intro">Card effects here are simplified and grouped by <em class="em-gold">where they activate</em> (hand, graveyard, or field), plus the archetype's signature on-Tribute triggers. Each entry adds tips &amp; tricks for real games.</p>

  {{ cardSearch(cards.total) }}
  {{ zoneFilter(cards.zones) }}
</section>

{{ sectionTabs(cards.groups, cards.total) }}

<section class="container-narrow groups">
  {% for g in cards.groups %}
  {{ cardGroup(g) }}
  {% endfor %}

  {{ filterEmpty() }}

  <details id="synergy" class="card-group" open>
    <summary class="group-head">
      <span class="group-dot" style="background:var(--zone-field);"></span>
      <h2>Expanding into other archetypes</h2>
    </summary>
    <p class="group-blurb">Mitsurugi runs no in-archetype locks, so it welcomes partners. These pair especially well.</p>
    <div class="synergy-grid">
      {% for a in cards.synergy %}
      {{ synergyCard(a) }}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="pending-note mono">More deck variants in progress: {{ cards.synergyPending | join(" · ") }}</p>
  </details>
</section>

<script src="{{ '/assets/js/card-filter.js' | url }}"></script>
